{#- The voice counterweight, appended to the post-history system message — the
    last message before generation, and so the closest available push-back
    against a cast that has started sounding like each other.

    Says "still outstanding" rather than "in the last scene": a flag survives a
    later not_enough verdict, and survives the character being off-cast for
    several scenes, so naming the last scene as the source would inject false
    chronology into the prompt.

    Renders only for present NPCs carrying an UNRESOLVED drift flag
    (store/voice_drift.py); a campaign whose cast is in voice renders nothing
    and costs nothing. Vars: voice_notes (list of {name, note}, non-empty). -#}
{%- if voice_notes | length == 1 -%}
{%- set n = voice_notes[0] -%}
{{ n.name }} has drifted out of voice, and the correction is still outstanding. {{ n.note }} Bring {{ n.name }} back to how they actually speak before anything else in this reply.
{%- else -%}
Some of the cast have drifted out of voice, with corrections still outstanding. Bring each of them back to how they actually speak before anything else in this reply.
{% for n in voice_notes %}
- {{ n.name }}: {{ n.note }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif -%}
